    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Pacific island democracy that gained full legislative independence in 1947 while keeping the British monarch as head of state.</li><li>It broke with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> over nuclear weapons in 1985–1987 and made its nuclear-free status law.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waitangi-tribunal">Waitangi Tribunal</a> and Treaty settlements since 1975 have reshaped relations between the Crown and Māori.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> adopted the Statute of Westminster only in 1947, sixteen years after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> passed it, and created its own citizenship from 1 January 1949.</p></aside>
    </section>

